eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-7 : List Word
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-7 = unlines (cons "In “Eye Contact: Co-Processing at the Speed of Light” (Part 7 of the Information Dynamic series), on eye contact: the coupling through light of the nervous systems of two people in visual range of each other, when both attend to each other:" (cons "Eye Contact: Mutual Active Co-Processing" (cons "When both people actively attend to each other—making eye contact—the coupling intensifies:" (cons "Both nervous systems are:" (cons "Sampling detailed information about the other (gaze direction, pupil state, facial micro-expressions)" (cons "Updating internal models based on observations" (cons "Modulating own behavior based on observed state" (cons "Aware of being observed while observing" (cons "This creates feedback loop:" (cons "Person A observes Person B's state" (cons "→ Person A updates model of B" (cons "→ Person A's state changes (informed by model update)" (cons "→ Person B observes Person A's state change" (cons "→ Person B updates model of A" (cons "→ Person B's state changes" (cons "→ Person A observes Person B's state change" (cons "→ Repeat continuously in real-time" (cons "The loop operates at speeds limited primarily by neural processing (~tens of milliseconds for conscious recognition), not by information transmission (which happens at near-light-speed). The bottleneck is computation, not communication." (cons "They are co-processing: Each nervous system is actively using the other as external information source, updating continuously, affecting each other's states through observation and response. The electromagnetic coupling creates informational bridge operating at near-minimum physically achievable latency." nil)))))))))))))))))))
